      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Standout Family Home with Style, Space and Exceptional Presentation comes to the open market with this four-bedroom end-of-terrace, B3 energy rating, approx 118.2 sq.m (1,272 sq.ft) built c.2007 this home combines modern elegance with everything a growing family needs. Throughout the property, modern décor and tasteful finishes create a bright, contemporary environment that is both stylish and practical, comprising of well-proportioned accommodation, complemented by a private rear garden and an attractive outlook over a large green.\n\nThe accommodation comprises of the entrance hallway, featuring bespoke-style wall panelling and a solid oak staircase, guest WC recently refurbished and tiled. The spacious sitting room has a front aspect with laminate flooring, bespoke fitted storage units and wall panelling, double doors leading to the fully fitted modern kitchen/dining room with a dual aspect and patio doors leading to the private rear garden. The first floor comprises of a carpeted landing with hot-press, side window aspect and Velux window. Four bedrooms, three with slide robes. The master with recently refurbished and retiled ensuite. Bedroom four is currently being used as a dressing room with built in storage and carpet flooring. The main family bathroom again has been recently refurbished and fully tiled.\n\nThe exterior of this home is equally as well maintained as the interior with tarmac driveway to the front offering ample car parking space, a private well fenced rear garden having an imprinted concrete patio area with patio lights, artificial lawn, enclosed oil tank, shed with concrete base and power supply, pedestrian gate to the side entrance.\n\nCastlepollard town centre which offers all necessary amenities including a selection of local shops, pubs, Church's, Tesco shopping centre, two primary schools and a post primary school, post office, library, Castlevaragh Hotel, two doctors' surgeries and the new playground. Within easy access of many lakes and rivers for water sport and fishing, Tullynally Castle, gardens and tea rooms for forestry walks on your door step. Lough Lene Blue Flag Lake in Collinstown is less than a 10-minute drive, famed for fishing, swimming and water sports. The historical village of Fore is just 6km from Castlepollard for local primary school, coffee shops, country pubs, visitors' centre and the Barrel & Bean distillery and café.\n\nCastlepollard is a key location for access in travel to Dublin on the M50 approx 40 mins, Mullingar approx 12km, other key routes include Athlone, Tullamore and Galway. Serviced with the New TFI Local Link 818 Mullingar to Castlepollard via Collinstown, offering 5 daily return services Monday to Thursday, 8 on Friday, 7 on Saturday and 5 on Sundays.\n\nViewing is highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation \nEntrance Hall 6.529m x 1.885m (21'5\" x 6'2\"): Welcoming entrance hallway with composite front door laminate flooring, wall panelling, solid oak stairs with built in storage.\n\nSitting Room 3.983m x 4.992m (13'1\" x 16'5\"): Lovely spacious sitting room with front aspect, laminate flooring, wall panelling, coving, solid fuel fireplace having built in storage units with downlights to either side, double doors to kitchen/dining room.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room\n4.611m x 3.885m (15'2\" x 12'9\"):\nModern fitted kitchen with wall and floor units offering ample work and storage space, tiled splash backs and tiled flooring, dual aspect, patio doors to the private rear garden.\n\nGuest WC 1.427m x 1.317m (4'8\" x 4'4\"): Recently refurbished and tiled with WC, wash hand basin, mirror, fan, radiator and window.\n\nLanding 2.109m x 4.170m (6'11\" x 13'8\"): Bright spacious landing with side window aspect and Velux window, carpet flooring, hot-press shelved with immersion, access to attic, wall panelling.\n\nBathroom 1.573m x 2m (5'2\" x 6'7\"):\nRecently refurbished and tiled walls and flooring, WC, wash hand basin with vanity unit, mirror, double shower cubicle, fan, heated towel rail, Velux window.\n\nBedroom One 2.996m x 2.366m (9'10\" x 7'9\"): Single room, rear aspect, TV point, slide robes, carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom Two 3.470m x 3.320m (11'5\" x 10'11\"): Double room, carpet flooring, slide robes, TV point, rear aspect.\n\nBedroom Three 2.807m x 2.218m (9'3\" x 7'3\"):\nFront aspect, carpet flooring, currently being used as a dressing room.\n\nBedroom Four 3.381m x 3.778m (11'1\" x 12'5\"): The master bedroom with elegant décor, front aspect, wall panelling, TV point, carpet flooring and slide robes.\n\nEnsuite 1.549m x1.670m (5'1\" x5'6\"):\nRecently refurbished and tiled walls and floor, WC, wash hand basin with vanity unit, shower cubicle with Triton T90SR electric unit, mirror, fan, heated towel rail.\n\nShed 3.5m x 3m (11'6\" x 9'10\"):\nWired, power socket, lights, concrete base, fuseboard.\n\nSpecial Features & Services\n•Oil Fired Central Heating\n•Solid fuel fireplace in sitting room\n•Modern interior\n•Recently refurbished and tiled bathrooms\n•Turn key condition\n•Triple glazed windows and doors fitted approx 1 year\n•Outside tap\n•Outside power socket\n•Private rear garden\n•Artificial lawn\n•Imprinted concrete patio\n•Paving lights\n•Side gate\n•Tarmac front driveway\n•Alarmed\n•Built c.2007\n•Approx 118.2 sq.m (1,272 sq.ft)\n•Walking distance to all amenities\n•Overlooking a large green\n•Approx 20 mins Mullingar\n•Approx 6km to Fore Village\n•Approx 8km to Collinstown Village\n•Approx 16km to Oldcastle\n\nIncluded in Sale\n•Dishwasher\n•Washing machine\n•Oven\n•Hob\n•Fridge\n•Extractor fan\n•Blinds\n•Curtains\n•Light fitting\n•Mirrors in bathrooms\n•Shed\n\nBER Details\nBER Rating:B3 BER No. 109792028"
